WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.650
- Apparently, there's a lot
of Bear Grylls fans out there.

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:04.180
You've asked me to watch the scenes,

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:06.840
comment on their medical
accuracy and safety,

00:00:08.393 --> 00:00:11.053
- [Bear] You'll need water,
but if there isn't any,

00:00:11.053 --> 00:00:12.753
you can drink your own pee.

00:00:12.753 --> 00:00:13.613
- No!

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:15.223
Bear, come on.

00:00:15.223 --> 00:00:17.203
PSA, do not drink your own pee.

00:00:17.203 --> 00:00:19.913
If you drink what your body excreted,

00:00:19.913 --> 00:00:22.423
especially if you're already
borderline dehydrated,

00:00:22.423 --> 00:00:24.073
you're gonna be getting
rid of all the stuff

00:00:24.073 --> 00:00:25.743
that you don't need and
then taking it back in.

00:00:25.743 --> 00:00:27.323
I know we sometimes say, urine is sterile.

00:00:27.323 --> 00:00:28.156
It's not.
(alarm blares)

00:00:28.156 --> 00:00:28.989
There's bacteria.

00:00:28.989 --> 00:00:29.943
Then you're gonna be drinking it?

00:00:29.943 --> 00:00:31.563
Now you're giving yourself diarrhea,

00:00:31.563 --> 00:00:33.593
potentially another fever-causing illness,

00:00:33.593 --> 00:00:35.393
which is gonna dehydrate you further.

00:00:35.393 --> 00:00:36.793
And there's other uses for your pee!

00:00:36.793 --> 00:00:38.843
Put it on your clothes
and put it on your skin,

00:00:38.843 --> 00:00:40.553
so that when it evaporates,
it cools you down.

00:00:40.553 --> 00:00:42.673
It might not smell great,
but you'll survive.

00:00:42.673 --> 00:00:43.506
Come on, Bear.

00:00:43.506 --> 00:00:45.034
- And if I just peed on the ground,

00:00:45.034 --> 00:00:47.183
that's all those fluids wasted.

00:00:47.183 --> 00:00:49.413
- They're not wasted
because fluid management

00:00:49.413 --> 00:00:52.093
within your body is not just fluids.

00:00:52.093 --> 00:00:54.363
It's fluids plus-minus electrolytes,

00:00:54.363 --> 00:00:55.983
and what your body does in urine is,

00:00:55.983 --> 00:00:59.293
it gets rid of those
electrolytes that it doesn't need

00:00:59.293 --> 00:01:01.403
and it keeps a very careful balance.

00:01:01.403 --> 00:01:03.383
When you drink your urine,

00:01:03.383 --> 00:01:05.133
you're essentially throwing that off

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:06.743
further and further each time.

00:01:06.743 --> 00:01:09.053
So, like, no. Do not drink urine.

00:01:09.053 --> 00:01:10.673
I'm gonna eat some Thrive seaweed

00:01:10.673 --> 00:01:12.753
while he drinks that urine.

00:01:12.753 --> 00:01:13.686
Also salty.

00:01:14.613 --> 00:01:15.933
Much tastier.

00:01:15.933 --> 00:01:18.703
- Not, not my favorite.

00:01:18.703 --> 00:01:21.783
- No? That's not the
Gatorade flavor you go for?

00:01:21.783 --> 00:01:24.633
- [Bear] Urine is actually 95% water,

00:01:24.633 --> 00:01:26.233
and it's sterile when fresh.

00:01:26.233 --> 00:01:28.953
- It's not, because it has
to go through your pee-hole,

00:01:28.953 --> 00:01:30.263
which sometimes has bacteria in it.

00:01:30.263 --> 00:01:32.673
- [Bear] And drink it
sooner rather than later,

00:01:32.673 --> 00:01:34.513
as it's a breeding ground for bacteria.

00:01:34.513 --> 00:01:36.523
- How does Bear Grylls say
that his urine is sterile,

00:01:36.523 --> 00:01:37.603
meaning it has no bacteria,

00:01:37.603 --> 00:01:39.413
then say it's a breeding
ground for bacteria?

00:01:39.413 --> 00:01:40.723
Where does the bacteria come from?

00:01:40.723 --> 00:01:42.893
- One thing you can do
if you're stuck out here

00:01:42.893 --> 00:01:44.433
with no water source at all--

00:01:44.433 --> 00:01:46.033
- Is not to drink your own urine.

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:49.513
- Is actually drink the fluid
from a fresh elephant dung.

00:01:49.513 --> 00:01:50.396
- Oh, my God!

00:01:50.396 --> 00:01:53.863
Does he just try and find
liquid anywhere he can?

00:01:53.863 --> 00:01:54.820
- Pretty disgusting--
- Yeah, it is!

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:56.823
- But it could save your life.

00:01:56.823 --> 00:01:58.263
- It's not,

00:01:58.263 --> 00:02:01.323
All of this is so
temporary, it's incredible.

00:02:01.323 --> 00:02:04.013
There is so much bacteria in that water

00:02:04.013 --> 00:02:06.983
that it will give you diarrhea,
thereby dehydrate you.

00:02:06.983 --> 00:02:08.763
This makes no sense.

00:02:08.763 --> 00:02:09.953
- Wow, I tell you what,

00:02:09.953 --> 00:02:13.713
these are the biggest
grubs I've ever seen.

00:02:13.713 --> 00:02:15.138
Look.

00:02:15.138 --> 00:02:17.653
And this is just the sort
of place that they like.

00:02:17.653 --> 00:02:19.583
They feed off all this rotting,

00:02:19.583 --> 00:02:21.603
soft interior of the palm tree.

00:02:21.603 --> 00:02:22.743
- Just think about that.

00:02:22.743 --> 00:02:24.053
Do you want to eat a bug

00:02:24.053 --> 00:02:28.393
that was just eating the
rotten interior of a palm tree?

00:02:28.393 --> 00:02:30.163
- And actually, the
locals eat a lot of these.

00:02:30.163 --> 00:02:31.703
They're like a delicacy.

00:02:31.703 --> 00:02:33.553
They're full of good protein.

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:36.533
- When he says "good
protein," does he mean it?

00:02:36.533 --> 00:02:39.793
- [Bear] It'll be worth every
one of its 140 calories.

00:02:39.793 --> 00:02:41.493
- Cook it, my guy.

00:02:41.493 --> 00:02:42.736
- Holy smoke.

00:02:43.582 --> 00:02:44.415
That is

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:46.097
just

00:02:51.183 --> 00:02:52.383
horrible.
- Yeah!

00:02:52.383 --> 00:02:53.733
- Do you know what?

00:02:53.733 --> 00:02:55.353
They can keep their delicacies.

00:02:55.353 --> 00:02:57.443
- Like, I've seen people eat insects,

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:58.633
and crickets, and stuff before.

00:02:58.633 --> 00:02:59.553
They do have protein.

00:02:59.553 --> 00:03:01.906
But, like, the cooking
part is just mandatory.

00:03:03.296 --> 00:03:04.129
Is that a camel?

00:03:04.129 --> 00:03:07.346
- What I'm looking for is the stomach.

00:03:08.633 --> 00:03:10.713
- How does he know the anatomy of animals?

00:03:10.713 --> 00:03:11.993
- It's in three parts,

00:03:11.993 --> 00:03:15.733
so it can separate the
liquids from the solids.

00:03:15.733 --> 00:03:16.566
- Wow.

00:03:16.566 --> 00:03:19.693
- And the bit I want is called the rumen.

00:03:19.693 --> 00:03:21.633
- I see the fascia there.

00:03:21.633 --> 00:03:24.543
- [Bear] This rumen water
is just like a reservoir.

00:03:24.543 --> 00:03:27.583
- What? (laughs) Oh, my God.

00:03:27.583 --> 00:03:31.353
I can't imagine that
that is safe to drink.

00:03:31.353 --> 00:03:35.673
- And a nomad told me once how his uncle,

00:03:35.673 --> 00:03:39.453
in the 1950s, was lost
in a sandstorm out here,

00:03:39.453 --> 00:03:42.723
and he actually ended up killing his camel

00:03:42.723 --> 00:03:45.753
to get at the rumen

00:03:45.753 --> 00:03:48.083
and all this fluid inside.

00:03:48.083 --> 00:03:48.916
- Oh!

00:03:48.916 --> 00:03:50.013
- And that actually saved his life.

00:03:50.013 --> 00:03:51.663
- As an evidence-based physician,

00:03:51.663 --> 00:03:53.843
I don't like hearing anecdotes like that,

00:03:53.843 --> 00:03:56.243
that some guy, one time, 200 years ago,

00:03:56.243 --> 00:03:57.863
saved his life by killing his camel.

00:03:57.863 --> 00:03:59.393
That, like, proves nothing to me.

00:03:59.393 --> 00:04:00.783
That story could've been made up.

00:04:00.783 --> 00:04:01.853
It could've been embellished.

00:04:01.853 --> 00:04:03.923
It doesn't mean that everyone
should be killing camels

00:04:03.923 --> 00:04:05.413
and drinking their rumen water.

00:04:05.413 --> 00:04:07.293
I don't know, it just,
it sounds so extreme.

00:04:07.293 --> 00:04:08.756
- [Bear] And look inside.

00:04:09.643 --> 00:04:11.643
You can see everything it's been eating.

00:04:12.863 --> 00:04:13.696
- Which is what?

00:04:13.696 --> 00:04:15.213
- And that is just--
- Grass?

00:04:15.213 --> 00:04:16.926
- Sort of, partially digested.

00:04:18.913 --> 00:04:21.643
And the fluid in this,
again, is dripping--

00:04:21.643 --> 00:04:25.153
- No! He's gonna drink the
gastric juices of a camel?

00:04:25.153 --> 00:04:26.806
No. Come on.

00:04:27.655 --> 00:04:29.793
Oh, my God!

00:04:29.793 --> 00:04:31.496
Bear Grylls is the type of guy,

00:04:32.763 --> 00:04:35.483
five million years ago,
to see a cow udder,

00:04:38.007 --> 00:04:39.627
- You can eat these things

00:04:39.627 --> 00:04:41.897
straight out of the river like that.

00:04:41.897 --> 00:04:43.917
- Oh, my God, what is he,

00:04:43.917 --> 00:04:45.677
it's like he does it on purpose.

00:04:45.677 --> 00:04:48.437
- [Bear] Just what my
body needs to keep moving.

00:04:48.437 --> 00:04:50.847
I'm gonna take full
advantage of this feast.

00:04:50.847 --> 00:04:54.267
- It's kinda weird to me that,
as a survival specialist,

00:04:54.267 --> 00:04:56.547
he makes no use of fire here.

00:04:56.547 --> 00:04:58.357
Fire was invented for a reason,

00:04:58.357 --> 00:05:00.907
to cook things, to prevent infections,

00:05:00.907 --> 00:05:03.717
because one of the leading
killers before fire,

00:05:03.717 --> 00:05:05.477
before the use of cooking our food,

00:05:05.477 --> 00:05:07.597
storing our food correctly, was diarrhea.

00:05:07.597 --> 00:05:08.727
It would dehydrate you.

00:05:08.727 --> 00:05:09.977
Electrolyte imbalance.

00:05:09.977 --> 00:05:10.810
Your heart would stop.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:11.917
Acute kidney failure.

00:05:11.917 --> 00:05:14.087
- [Bear] I've noticed a
lot of bees in the area,

00:05:14.087 --> 00:05:15.567
so I'm heading through the scrub

00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:17.547
to get to the hive and find some honey.

00:05:17.547 --> 00:05:18.917
- You know I'm a honey fan.

00:05:18.917 --> 00:05:20.177
Like, I love honey.

00:05:20.177 --> 00:05:21.907
Honey works as good, or better,

00:05:21.907 --> 00:05:23.827
than over-the-counter cough suppressants

00:05:23.827 --> 00:05:25.278
in the pediatric population.

00:05:25.278 --> 00:05:29.177
(tense music)
(bees buzzing)

00:05:29.177 --> 00:05:30.657
Oh, that looks fresh.

00:05:30.657 --> 00:05:32.487
Fresh honeycomb.

00:05:32.487 --> 00:05:35.467
- [Bear] Leaving my forehead
exposed was a real oversight.

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:37.837
- If you get a really bad sting,

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:39.387
and you happen to be an individual

00:05:39.387 --> 00:05:41.737
who is severely allergic to a bee sting,

00:05:41.737 --> 00:05:42.907
you go into anaphylactic shock,

00:05:42.907 --> 00:05:45.067
where your throat closes up,
your blood pressure drops.

00:05:45.067 --> 00:05:47.387
That could be lethal very, very quickly.

00:05:47.387 --> 00:05:49.447
That's why if you know
you have an allergy,

00:05:49.447 --> 00:05:52.197
you should have an EpiPen, like
that, on hand at all times,

00:05:52.197 --> 00:05:53.197
and not necessarily an EpiPen,

00:05:53.197 --> 00:05:55.687
any kind of epinephrine autoinjector.

00:05:55.687 --> 00:05:57.957
Oh, he's swelling.

00:05:57.957 --> 00:06:00.027
- The bee sting has made all of, you know,

00:06:00.027 --> 00:06:00.860
this part of me swell up.

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:01.697
Allergic reactions can be fatal.

00:06:01.697 --> 00:06:03.927
- That's serious edema right there.

00:06:03.927 --> 00:06:06.207
- I'm worried about anaphylactic shock,

00:06:06.207 --> 00:06:08.717
the first signs of
swelling around the eyes,

00:06:08.717 --> 00:06:11.877
followed by difficulty breathing
and loss of consciousness.

00:06:11.877 --> 00:06:14.817
- These type of large
reactions are really treated

00:06:14.817 --> 00:06:17.667
with supportive care if it's
not true anaphylactic shock.

00:06:17.667 --> 00:06:19.157
You wanna think cold compresses,

00:06:19.157 --> 00:06:21.037
steroids in serious cases,

00:06:21.037 --> 00:06:22.417
and really just making sure

00:06:22.417 --> 00:06:24.627
that the patient's
airway's not compromised,

00:06:24.627 --> 00:06:26.357
their blood pressure remains stable.

00:06:26.357 --> 00:06:29.927
Once that's okay, that usually
does pass in a few days.

00:06:29.927 --> 00:06:33.157
But swelling on its own, if
it's not over the airway,

00:06:33.157 --> 00:06:35.017
is not intrinsically dangerous.

00:06:35.017 --> 00:06:37.437
- [Bear] I'm on a raft
in the Pacific Ocean.

00:06:37.437 --> 00:06:39.104
I've collected some fresh water,

00:06:39.104 --> 00:06:41.827
but it's full of bird
droppings and it's rancid.

00:06:41.827 --> 00:06:43.787
Drink this, and you'd probably vomit,

00:06:43.787 --> 00:06:45.947
and risk worsening dehydration.

00:06:45.947 --> 00:06:48.127
But there is a way of using it

00:06:48.127 --> 00:06:49.977
to gain life-giving fluids,

00:06:49.977 --> 00:06:51.557
but only as a last resort.

00:06:51.557 --> 00:06:52.790
- I don't even know what he's about to do,

00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:55.797
but the fact that it has
bird droppings makes me think

00:06:55.797 --> 00:06:57.247
that there's so much E. coli in it,

00:06:57.247 --> 00:06:59.887
that if it makes any contact
with the inside of your body,

00:06:59.887 --> 00:07:01.607
whether it's through a
cut or you drinking it,

00:07:01.607 --> 00:07:03.327
you're just gonna get a massive infection.

00:07:03.327 --> 00:07:04.487
And a massive infection,

00:07:04.487 --> 00:07:06.497
when you're stranded
and you're surviving is,

00:07:06.497 --> 00:07:08.877
like, the worst case scenario.

00:07:08.877 --> 00:07:10.421
- [Bear] I'm gonna give myself an enema.

00:07:10.421 --> 00:07:12.817
- (laughs) Oh, my God!

00:07:12.817 --> 00:07:14.357
He doesn't try and survive.

00:07:14.357 --> 00:07:15.190
He's gotta think,

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:18.437
"What is the most ridiculous,
extreme thing I can do

00:07:18.437 --> 00:07:19.767
in order to make this show?"

00:07:19.767 --> 00:07:22.497
Could you absorb fluids from your rectum?

00:07:22.497 --> 00:07:24.557
Yes, there are small blood vessels there.

00:07:24.557 --> 00:07:26.017
We do give suppositories there,

00:07:26.017 --> 00:07:28.747
so there are absorptive qualities there.

00:07:28.747 --> 00:07:30.387
Oh, my God, I can't believe
I'm even thinking about this.

00:07:30.387 --> 00:07:32.917
There's also a lot of bacteria
that lives in your rectum,

00:07:32.917 --> 00:07:36.577
including E. coli, which
doesn't enter your bloodstream.

00:07:36.577 --> 00:07:39.277
So, it could be an okay
place to have some bacteria.

00:07:39.277 --> 00:07:41.747
There's just so much that could go wrong.

00:07:41.747 --> 00:07:43.287
I think it's, like, a 50/50 shot.

00:07:43.287 --> 00:07:46.701
Will you survive, or will
you kill yourself further?

00:07:46.701 --> 00:07:49.507
- Now, that's placenta.

00:07:49.507 --> 00:07:50.340
- Oh, my God.

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:51.977
- Did somebody have a baby?
- Is that Shaq?

00:07:51.977 --> 00:07:54.307
- What's rare, though,
is find it so fresh.

00:07:54.307 --> 00:07:56.377
That, for me, is good news.

00:07:56.377 --> 00:07:57.297
- Is it good news?

00:07:57.297 --> 00:07:59.137
- [Bear] It looks, actually, like dinner.

00:07:59.137 --> 00:08:00.597
- Shaq, don't do it, buddy.

00:08:00.597 --> 00:08:01.977
I've seen you three-peat.

00:08:01.977 --> 00:08:05.310
- And this is a first
for me, to eat placenta.

00:08:06.627 --> 00:08:08.490
- Yeah, it should be a last.

00:08:10.325 --> 00:08:11.987
(placenta sizzles)

00:08:11.987 --> 00:08:13.537
Like, there are some
cultures that do this,

00:08:13.537 --> 00:08:16.137
because the placenta is,
like, it has the nutrients,

00:08:16.137 --> 00:08:18.277
and it does the oxygen distribution

00:08:18.277 --> 00:08:20.107
for the baby through the umbilical cord,

00:08:20.107 --> 00:08:21.927
and there's some cultures
that think about doing this.

00:08:21.927 --> 00:08:24.467
But, like, the CDC has put
out a specific warning,

00:08:24.467 --> 00:08:25.447
like, do not do this.

00:08:25.447 --> 00:08:28.767
If you get a group B strep
infection in your placenta,

00:08:28.767 --> 00:08:29.600
and then you eat it,

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:31.287
and then you pass it to your
baby through breast milk,

00:08:31.287 --> 00:08:32.120
that's deadly.

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:33.297
That's lethal to a newborn.

00:08:36.347 --> 00:08:37.607
I give him props.

00:08:37.607 --> 00:08:39.036
I wouldn't do it.

00:08:39.036 --> 00:08:41.547
(Shaq spits)
- (laughs) Shaq is my man.

00:08:41.547 --> 00:08:43.857
- [Bear] It's traditional for Berber men

00:08:43.857 --> 00:08:45.917
to eat goats' testicles.

00:08:45.917 --> 00:08:47.957
They're thought to enhance fertility,

00:08:47.957 --> 00:08:50.337
and it's certainly gonna
be a test of my manhood.

00:08:50.337 --> 00:08:52.147
- Look, I'm respective of all cultures.

00:08:52.147 --> 00:08:54.527
The line I draw is medical misinformation.

00:08:54.527 --> 00:08:56.447
If you're gonna tell
me eating a goat's nut

00:08:56.447 --> 00:08:58.697
is gonna help you get fertile,

00:08:58.697 --> 00:08:59.627
I'm not gonna buy it.

00:08:59.627 --> 00:09:01.800
I need evidence-based medicine for that.

00:09:04.547 --> 00:09:05.380
Why raw?

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:07.127
Just put it over a flame.

00:09:07.127 --> 00:09:09.618
- [Bear] Well, that's
definitely a first for me.

00:09:09.618 --> 00:09:11.197
(Bear retching)
- See, he's throwing up,

00:09:11.197 --> 00:09:13.257
because there's bacteria and it's gross.

00:09:13.257 --> 00:09:16.217
- And what this stuff
is, is like sunblock.

00:09:16.217 --> 00:09:17.067
- Oh, wow.

00:09:17.067 --> 00:09:19.617
- And the coral, itself,
we use, it's at low tide.

00:09:19.617 --> 00:09:21.327
When it's exposed to the sun,

00:09:21.327 --> 00:09:24.217
it will secrete this as a
way of protecting itself.

00:09:24.217 --> 00:09:25.617
Just amazing.
- Wow.

00:09:25.617 --> 00:09:27.987
- Scientists have actually
reckoned this stuff

00:09:27.987 --> 00:09:29.787
is as good as factor 50.

00:09:29.787 --> 00:09:32.267
- Wow, an SPF 50's
pretty great protection.

00:09:32.267 --> 00:09:34.847
I mean, I always say get
the highest SPF possible,

00:09:34.847 --> 00:09:37.587
even though once you get above
50, not much is changing.

00:09:37.587 --> 00:09:39.957
That's only if you're
following the exact guidelines,

00:09:39.957 --> 00:09:42.024
and I don't know about
this whole mushroom thing,

00:09:42.024 --> 00:09:43.947
but just get the one from the store.

00:09:43.947 --> 00:09:46.027
- [Bear] If it's got tentacles like that,

00:09:46.027 --> 00:09:47.577
those are stingers.

00:09:47.577 --> 00:09:48.727
But--
- So you can't eat it?

00:09:48.727 --> 00:09:49.723
- Jellyfish scare me.

00:09:49.723 --> 00:09:51.137
- You can eat the body of it.
- Right.

00:09:51.137 --> 00:09:51.970
- Foil it out.

00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:53.900
And it's a bit like,

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:55.337
tastes a little bit like gelatine.

00:09:55.337 --> 00:09:56.517
It's pure protein.

00:09:56.517 --> 00:09:58.387
- I don't know what the deal
is with eating jellyfish.

00:09:58.387 --> 00:10:00.937
I missed that day in
residency in a medical school.

00:10:00.937 --> 00:10:03.607
Folks, today, we're learning
about eating jellyfish.

00:10:03.607 --> 00:10:05.925
It's like peanut butter
and jelly, but with fish.

00:10:05.925 --> 00:10:07.278
- And those are the,

00:10:07.278 --> 00:10:08.111
those,

00:10:08.111 --> 00:10:09.568
(Bear yelps)

00:10:09.568 --> 00:10:11.337
- It got you?
- Yeah.

00:10:11.337 --> 00:10:12.597
- So he got stung by a jellyfish,

00:10:12.597 --> 00:10:13.927
- Oh! He put it in his mouth?

00:10:13.927 --> 00:10:14.760
- I've seen movies before

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:16.557
where if somebody gets
stung by a jellyfish,

00:10:16.557 --> 00:10:17.427
you have to pee on them.

00:10:17.427 --> 00:10:19.617
- The whole thing with
peeing on a jellyfish sting,

00:10:19.617 --> 00:10:23.387
really comes from preventing
the discharge of more toxin,

00:10:23.387 --> 00:10:24.877
and creating more inflammation.

00:10:24.877 --> 00:10:27.067
The general consensus has
been to use sea water,

00:10:27.067 --> 00:10:29.037
and not to use fresh water, especially,

00:10:29.037 --> 00:10:31.157
'cause it can cause more of
that toxin to be released.

00:10:31.157 --> 00:10:33.497
- If you just relax, then I'll relax,

00:10:33.497 --> 00:10:34.757
now I've got stage fright.

00:10:34.757 --> 00:10:36.537
- I can't relax.

00:10:36.537 --> 00:10:38.897
- To pee on demand when
somebody is in pain

00:10:38.897 --> 00:10:40.127
is very difficult.

00:10:40.127 --> 00:10:43.057
- Peeing is actually a
complex, neurologic process.

00:10:43.057 --> 00:10:44.607
It's very easy to throw that off.

00:10:44.607 --> 00:10:46.817
If, for example, you've had a stroke,

00:10:46.817 --> 00:10:48.007
if you've had an injury to that area,

00:10:48.007 --> 00:10:51.467
it's very easy to develop
urinary incontinence,

00:10:51.467 --> 00:10:53.557
or urinary retention, and sometimes,

00:10:53.557 --> 00:10:56.067
the treatment for that,
is actually biofeedback,

00:10:56.067 --> 00:10:59.217
and understanding how to
control different muscles

00:10:59.217 --> 00:11:00.050
in the area.

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:03.697
- I've been in water this cold before.

00:11:03.697 --> 00:11:05.060
- Oh, he's going swimming in cold water.

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:06.757
- It's plain horrible.

00:11:06.757 --> 00:11:08.747
- Yeah, it's horrible
just getting undressed.

00:11:08.747 --> 00:11:10.220
- Chilly Perkins.

00:11:11.077 --> 00:11:13.857
Okay. Well, I'm hooked up to
this transmitter, as well,

00:11:13.857 --> 00:11:15.977
and that should show you my heart rate,

00:11:15.977 --> 00:11:17.427
but also, my breathing rate.

00:11:17.427 --> 00:11:18.417
- Generally what happens is,

00:11:18.417 --> 00:11:20.397
when you hit really cold
temperatures like that,

00:11:20.397 --> 00:11:21.347
or go under water,

00:11:21.347 --> 00:11:23.587
lot of times you'll
have this diving reflex,

00:11:23.587 --> 00:11:25.717
where your body will
automatically send you

00:11:25.717 --> 00:11:27.157
into a bradycardic rhythm,

00:11:27.157 --> 00:11:28.847
where the electrical
activity of your heart

00:11:28.847 --> 00:11:31.504
actually slows down,
to allow you to survive

00:11:31.504 --> 00:11:33.227
longer under water.

00:11:33.227 --> 00:11:34.747
We actually used to use
this type of treatment

00:11:34.747 --> 00:11:36.587
for supraventricular tachycardia,

00:11:36.587 --> 00:11:38.467
where we actually got patients to perform

00:11:38.467 --> 00:11:40.537
this diving reflex, vagal maneuver,

00:11:40.537 --> 00:11:43.127
and it would reset their
heart rhythm, slow it down.

00:11:43.127 --> 00:11:45.227
Obviously needs to be
very carefully monitored.

00:11:45.227 --> 00:11:47.257
And now, with the new medications
that we have on board,

00:11:47.257 --> 00:11:50.133
we generally don't have to do this.

00:11:50.133 --> 00:11:52.937
(water splashes)
Oh! I'm cold for him.

00:11:52.937 --> 00:11:54.687
I'm cold for him!

00:11:54.687 --> 00:11:56.407
- [Bear] Watch, as my heart rate drops

00:11:56.407 --> 00:11:59.307
from 160 beats per minute to 55.

00:11:59.307 --> 00:12:00.417
- Yep, diving reflex.

00:12:00.417 --> 00:12:02.417
- It's known as a mammalian dive reflex.

00:12:02.417 --> 00:12:06.377
It gives you vital, extra
seconds to make it for surface.

00:12:06.377 --> 00:12:08.417
- He did it! See, it worked,

00:12:08.417 --> 00:12:09.867
his survival mechanism kicked in.

00:12:09.867 --> 00:12:13.247
We also actually use hypothermia
treatment in patients

00:12:13.247 --> 00:12:15.767
who are undergoing
prolonged cardiac arrest,

00:12:15.767 --> 00:12:17.517
where we realize that
if we put them through

00:12:17.517 --> 00:12:19.497
a hypothermia protocol, very controlled,

00:12:19.497 --> 00:12:22.757
we actually decrease the
oxygen demand on the body,

00:12:22.757 --> 00:12:23.807
on certain organs,

00:12:23.807 --> 00:12:27.177
therefore we give them a little
bit longer survival time.

00:12:27.177 --> 00:12:29.197
Bear Grylls certainly
does a lot of cool stuff

00:12:29.197 --> 00:12:30.030
on the ground,

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:32.387
but I just flew an F-16 in the sky,

00:12:32.387 --> 00:12:34.437
here's what happens to your
body when you're flying

00:12:34.437 --> 00:12:36.677
in an F-16 and experiencing a lot of G's.

00:12:37.931 --> 00:12:40.172
As always, stay happy and healthy.

00:12:40.172 --> 00:12:42.755
(upbeat music)

